      "servingTime": "40-45 minutes",
      "yield": "4-6 servings",
      "tips": "",
      "ingredients": "For the Cookie Dough Layer\n1/2 cup unsalted butter, softened\n1/2 cup granulated sugar\n1/4 cup brown sugar\n1 large egg\n1 tsp. vanilla extract\n1 1/4 cups all-purpose flour\n1/2 tsp. baking soda\n1/4 tsp. salt\n1/2 cup Gold Rush Kit Kat bars, chopped\nFor the Brownie Layer\n1/2 cup unsalted butter\n1/2 cup granulated sugar\n1/2 cup brown sugar\n2 large eggs\n1 tsp. vanilla extract\n1/3 cup cocoa powder\n1/2 cup all-purpose flour\n1/4 tsp. baking powder\n1/4 tsp. salt\nToppings\n1-2 Gold Crush Kit Kat bars, chopped\n2-3 scoops of chocolate ice cream",
      "procedure": "Preheat your oven to 175°C. Lightly grease a 10-inch cast iron skillet.\nMake the Cookie Layer: In a mixing bowl, cream together butter, granulated sugar, and brown sugar until fluffy. Add egg and vanilla extract; mix until combined.\nIn a separate bowl, whisk together flour, baking soda, and salt. Gradually add to the wet ingredients. Fold in the chopped Kit Kat Gold Crush bars. Set aside.\nPrepare the Brownie Layer: In a microwave-safe bowl, melt butter and whisk in granulated sugar and brown sugar until smooth.Add eggs and vanilla extract; mix until glossy.\nSift in cocoa powder, flour, baking powder, and salt. Mix until just combined.\nAssemble the Brookie: Spread the brownie batter evenly into the skillet. Gently press chunks of cookie dough over the brownie layer to create a marbled effect.\nBake in the preheated oven for 25-30 minutes, or until the edges are set but the center remains slightly gooey.\nWhile still warm, top the brookie with chopped Kit Kat Gold Crush bars. \nAdd scoops of chocolate ice cream to the center of the skillet. Serve immediately with spoons for sharing!"
