      "procedure": "Toast the chopped pecans in a small pan over medium heat for 2-3 minutes. Add brown sugar and ground cinnamon, stirring until the sugar melts and coats the pecans. Remove from heat and let cool on a plate.\nBrew a shot of espresso or prepare 1 oz of strong brewed coffee. Let it cool slightly to prevent melting the ice.\nPour 1/4 cup of So Good Barista Oat Milk into a jar or milk frother. If using a jar, tightly seal it and shake vigorously for 30-60 seconds until foam forms. If using a frother, froth until creamy and airy. Set the foam aside.\nFill a tall glass with ice cubes. Pour the cooled espresso over the ice. Stir in the maple syrup to sweeten. Slowly pour remaining 1 cup of So Good Barista Oat Milk over the coffee. \nSpoon the oat milk foam on top of the iced latte. Sprinkle the prepared pecan crunch over the foam."
